<p>
  This Cookies Policy explains how ONYX uses cookies and similar local storage on this
  website. We keep this deliberately minimal.
</p>

<h2>1. Do we use tracking cookies?</h2>
<p><strong>No.</strong> This site does not use advertising cookies, analytics pixels, or
  cross-site trackers. We don’t profile you or sell your data.</p>

<h2>2. What we do store</h2>
<p>We use your browser’s <strong>local storage</strong> for two essential, functional purposes
  only:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Cookie choice</strong> — remembers whether you accepted or declined the notice,
    so we don’t ask again.</li>
  <li><strong>Intro preference</strong> — remembers you’ve seen the opening animation so it
    doesn’t replay every visit.</li>
</ul>
<p>This information stays in your browser, on your device. It is not sent to us or to any third
  party.</p>

<h2>3. Third-party requests</h2>
<p>When the page loads, your browser fetches fonts and script libraries from third-party
  networks (Google Fonts, cdnjs, jsDelivr). These providers may receive your IP address as a
  normal part of serving those files. They do not set tracking cookies on our behalf.</p>

<h2>4. Managing storage</h2>
<p>You can clear local storage at any time through your browser settings, and use the
  “Decline” option on the cookie notice. Declining does not break the site — the storage we
  use is functional, not tracking.</p>

<h2>5. More information</h2>
<p>See our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> for how we handle personal data, or email
  <a href="mailto:<%= site.email %>"><%= site.email %></a>.</p>
